# Shared Drives this project may search

## What to write here

Which Google Shared Drives the service account can actually see, and which of
them `/cs-find-document` is allowed to search for {{ company_name }}.

`cs drive search` is pinned to one scope (`CS_DRIVE`, `cs config` prints the
value in force){% if drive_scope %} — here, `{{ drive_scope }}`{% endif %}. But a service account often ends up
shared on more drives than that: a partner's folder, an archive, a personal
drive somebody added it to. List them, and for each say plainly whether it may
be searched from this project or must never be.

Also worth a line: where the documents customers ask for actually live, so the
skill starts in the right place instead of crawling.

## Why it matters

`/cs-find-document` searches on behalf of {{ email_address }} and quotes what it
finds back to a customer. A drive belonging to somebody else that nobody wrote
down here is a drive it may search in good faith — and a leak that looks, from
the outside, exactly like {{ company_name }} sending a stranger's document to a
customer.
